{"tool_name":"hemi","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"hemi","home":"http://hemi.biocuckoo.org/down.php","summary":"Toolkit for illustrating heatmaps.","addition_date":"2018-05-19T17:40:45Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:58Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:hemi","credit":[{"email":"xueyu@mail.hust.edu.cn","name":"Dr. Yu Xue","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://hemi.biocuckoo.org/download/HemI_Manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Heat map generation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0531"}]}],"name":"HemI","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/JOURNAL.PONE.0111988","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2014 Deng et al.Recent high-throughput techniques have generated a flood of biological data in all aspects. The transformation and visualization of multi-dimensional and numerical gene or protein expression data in a single heatmap can provide a concise but comprehensive presentation of molecular dynamics under different conditions. In this work, we developed an easy-to-use tool named HemI (Heat map Illustrator), which can visualize either gene or protein expression data in heatmaps. Additionally, the heatmaps can be recolored, rescaled or rotated in a customized manner. In addition, HemI provides multiple clustering strategies for analyzing the data. Publication-quality figures can be exported directly. We propose that HemI can be a useful toolkit for conveniently visualizing and manipulating heatmaps. The stand-alone packages of HemI were implemented in Java and can be accessed at http://hemi.biocuckoo.org/down.php.","authors":[{"name":"Cheng H."},{"name":"Deng W."},{"name":"Liu Z."},{"name":"Wang Y."},{"name":"Xue Y."}],"citationCount":672,"date":"2014-11-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS ONE","title":"HemI: A toolkit for illustrating heatmaps"},"pmcid":"PMC4221433","pmid":"25372567"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0092"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Protein expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0108"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"HemI","home":"https://bio.tools/hemi","summary":"Toolkit for illustrating heatmaps.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:hemi/app/hemi.biocuckoo.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":479,"citations":[{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":8,"year":"2015"},{"count":9,"year":"2025"},{"count":11,"year":"2024"},{"count":28,"year":"2023"},{"count":30,"year":"2016"},{"count":55,"year":"2022"},{"count":58,"year":"2021"},{"count":60,"year":"2020"},{"count":66,"year":"2017"},{"count":72,"year":"2019"},{"count":78,"year":"2018"}],"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0111988","pmcid":"PMC4221433","pmid":"25372567","ref_count":10,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"}],"title":"HemI: a toolkit for illustrating heatmaps.","year":2014}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":500,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/hemi","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":500,"ssl":nu